  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-7155</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In a bid to reduce the gender gap, Oxfam in Nigeria has been implementing several projects to build the adaptive capacity of women especially, to influence change at all levels- family, community, local government, and even the state level. Oxfam in Nigeria has also continued to integrate gender across all its projects and programmes, through targeted gender programming interventions like mainstreaming of Gender Action Learning System to raise the consciousness of both women and men, boys and girls in our project intervention communities;  mainstreaming of Rapid Care Analysis into our projects and programmes to address the impact of unpaid care work on women to enable equal trickle-down effect of the expected outputs of our programmes and projects.
The objectives are to:
1) Stimulate grassroots movement of active citizens for the promotion of accountable and responsible governance systems (household, community, Local/State),
2) Raise a platform of inclusive voices that advocate for reforms on human rights and gender justice at community, state, and national levels,
3) Promote gender justice and women&apos;s economic empowerment through responsive government policies.

The Proposed Interventions will among Other Things:
&#x2022; Organize events that call for collective actions (with the participation of male gender champions), led by women networks and coalition to make demands to local authorities and account for socio-economic and gender injustices.
&#x2022; Strengthen the capacity of partners, women, and youths on local government and community policy influencing, advocacy,and gender responsive budgeting.
&#x2022; Train and build the capacity of women and youths on engender transformative leadership, political participation, and active citizenship with the purpose of laying the ground for more women&#x2019;s participation in councillorship and chairmanship in their LGA in the next 2023 elections
&#x2022; Establish strategic partnerships with women&#x2019;s rights organizations and key gender stakeholders through the observance of strategic international gender days (e.g. International Women&#x2019;s Day, International Day ofthe Girl Child, 16 Days of Activism Against Gender Based Violence &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; International Human Rights Day)
&#x2022; Support in-country gender assessments/analysis to identify the genderintegration gaps within our projects and programmes and proffer targeted recommendations to close identified gender gaps.</narrative>
  </description>
